@startuml
title Student – Check in to Event
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam maxMessageSize 230
skinparam ParticipantPadding 12
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #154a9b
  ParticipantBorderColor #154a9b
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #edf3fc
  GroupBorderColor #8a9eb8
  LifeLineBorderColor #8a9eb8
}

actor "Student" as U
boundary "User Interface" as UI
control "Attendance API" as API
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Background Processing\nOutbox / RabbitMQ / Worker" as BG

U -> UI : 1: Confirm QR check-in
UI -> UI : 1.1: Get device location
break [Location unavailable]
  UI --> U : 1.2: Display error; end attempt
end

UI -> API : 2: Submit QR token and location
activate API
API -> API : 2.1: Validate permission, GPS, QR,\nsession and student profile
break [Invalid request or service unavailable]
  API --> UI : 2.2: Return error
  UI --> U : 2.3: Display error
end
API -> DB : 2.4: Save PENDING request + Outbox\nin one transaction
break [Persistence fails]
  API --> UI : 2.5: Return error; request not accepted
end
API --> UI : 2.6: 202 – Accepted for processing
deactivate API

BG -> DB : 3: Relay reads Outbox; delivers request\nvia RabbitMQ to worker
BG -> DB : 3.1: Worker checks request, registration,\nsession, direction and GPS
alt [Validation passes]
  BG -> DB : 3.2: Record attendance if absent;\nsave ACCEPTED + processed Outbox
  BG -> DB : 3.3: Sync Conduct Score after commit
else [Validation fails]
  BG -> DB : 3.4: Save REJECTED, reason\nand processed Outbox
end
BG ->> API : 3.5: Publish result via Redis Pub/Sub

API ->> UI : 4: Notify change via SSE
UI -> API : 4.1: Fetch request status
API -> DB : 4.2: Read this student's own result
DB --> API : 4.3: Status and reason
API --> UI : 4.4: Return result
UI --> U : 4.5: Display accepted / rejected result

note over UI,API
  While PENDING, the client also polls every 1.5 seconds.
  SSE and background processing are independent; 202 is not final attendance success.
end note
@enduml
